Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:20:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: enable CPU thermal zone


Local T1100: the MT6771 thermal controller is MT8183-compatible, but the
MT6771 efuse calibration is not decoded (the driver falls back to defaults).
Enable only the CPU zone with trips 80/90/115 C; the other inherited MT8183
zones stay disabled until their sensors/calibration are validated.

---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index ee18af4..324ca31 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -1137,3 +1137,35 @@
 		amp-gpios = <&pio 159 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	};
 };
+
+
+/*
+ * T1100 thermal: the MT6771 thermal controller is register-compatible with
+ * the MT8183 AUXADC block, but the MT6771 efuse calibration is not decoded by
+ * the mainline driver (it falls back to the default calibration).  Use one
+ * CPU zone with conservative trips so the CPU can throttle before the critical
+ * shutdown point; leave the other MT8183 zones disabled until their sensors and
+ * calibration are validated.
+ */
+&cpu_thermal {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&threshold {
+	temperature = <80000>;
+};
+
+&target {
+	temperature = <90000>;
+};
+
+&cpu_crit {
+	temperature = <115000>;
+};
+
+&tzts1 { status = "disabled"; };
+&tzts2 { status = "disabled"; };
+&tzts3 { status = "disabled"; };
+&tzts4 { status = "disabled"; };
+&tzts5 { status = "disabled"; };
+&tztsABB { status = "disabled"; };
-- 
